const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can L\'okawa book my gorilla permit for me?', a: 'Yes. When you confirm your safari booking and pay the deposit, we immediately purchase your gorilla permit from the Uganda Wildlife Authority on your behalf. You do not need to contact UWA directly. We provide permit confirmation documentation once issued.' },
  { q: 'Are permits ever available at short notice?', a: 'Occasionally, yes. Cancellations do occur and UWA sometimes releases returned permits. In the low season (April and May) permits can be available with 2 to 4 weeks notice. We monitor availability and can often secure last-minute permits for clients with flexible dates.' },
  { q: 'What happens if the gorillas cannot be found on my trek day?', a: 'This is extremely rare. UWA rangers track the gorilla families\' position the evening before every trek using GPS data. The success rate for finding gorillas is consistently above 99% at Bwindi. In the extremely unlikely event gorillas are not found, UWA policy is to offer a complimentary permit for the following day.' },
  { q: 'Can children do gorilla trekking?', a: 'Children must be at least 15 years old to participate in gorilla trekking, per UWA regulations. This protects the gorillas from childhood diseases and ensures all participants can manage the physical demands. There is no upper age limit, and many seniors in their 70s and 80s successfully complete the trek.' },
];

